# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# Testing / tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Generated data (regenerate with scripts/generate_gridworld_data.py)
data/*.h5
results/*

# ...except the difficulty-calibration artifact, which is a published *measurement*
# rather than an intermediate: it is what the repo now cites for "does the difficulty
# knob do anything", and tests/test_v3/test_difficulty_calibration_artifact.py pins its
# headline numbers so they cannot drift out of the docs. Re-including it needs
# `results/*` above rather than `results/` -- git cannot re-include a path whose parent
# directory is itself excluded.
!results/difficulty_calibration/

# ...and the replication draws, for the same reason: leaderboard/v5_replicated.json
# reports intervals, and an interval whose underlying draws are not published is not
# checkable. These 20 files ARE the evidence that the intervals are non-degenerate.
!results/replication/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Paper source, internal planning docs, and dev/pilot scratch code are kept
# out of this repo intentionally (see CHANGELOG.md v1.3.0). Result figures
# used by the paper live in docs/figures/ and remain tracked.
/paper/

# The NeurIPS Evaluations & Datasets submission, held out for the same reason as /paper/
# plus one of its own: the track is DOUBLE-BLIND, and this repository is public and
# attributable. A submission sitting in an authored public repo during review is an
# anonymity problem that is far easier to avoid than to undo. It lives in the local
# archive alongside the extended version.
/paper_neurips/

# The Croissant metadata for that submission, for the same reason and then one more.
# The submission is anonymized: the dataset and its authors carry review pseudonyms.
# Those pseudonyms are only protective while they appear nowhere alongside the real
# name, so the file that defines them must not be committed to the repo that carries
# the real name -- and neither must anything quoting them, this comment included. Same
# hazard as /paper_neurips/, running the other direction. The deposit archive itself is
# already covered by dist/ above.
/croissant.json

/experiments/
/docs/internal/
/.worktrees/

# Disk layer under the families' calibration memoization (src/rhob/v3/calibration_cache.py).
# Deliberately NOT committed: a stale calibration does not fail loudly, it silently
# changes the physics under every published number. Keying it on a hash of the defining
# module makes a stale hit almost impossible, but "almost" is the wrong standard for a
# file that would be trusted forever once merged. CI restores it via actions/cache,
# where a wrong key costs a recomputation rather than a wrong result.
/.rhob_cache/
